---
import EvidenceImage from './EvidenceImage.astro';
import {photo} from '../data/evidence';
import '../styles/shipping-checklist.css';
const topics=[
 ['Part protection','Cosmetic faces, sealing surfaces, threads, fragile edges, cleanliness and corrosion-protection needs.','Protective materials, separation between parts, carton or case requirements and packing limits.'],
 ['Pack identification','Part number, drawing revision, quantity per pack, batch identification and required labels.','Whether labels, lot references and inspection documents are available in your requested format.'],
 ['Delivery basis','Full delivery address, receiving contact, required arrival date, requested trade term/version and named place.','Who books transport and handles export/import clearance, insurance, duties, taxes and local delivery.'],
 ['Documents','The document list required by procurement, logistics or your destination-side import contact.','Which documents are available for this order and who prepares each. Requirements depend on the destination and transaction.'],
 ['Schedule','Separate your required arrival date from the desired dispatch date.','Production takes 7–14 business days after drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing. Estimate transit separately.'],
];
const archive=['shipment-2022-order-packing','shipment-2022-prepared-load','shipping-example'];
---
<article class="sh-page">
 <header class="sh-hero"><div class="sh-hero-copy"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="sh-breadcrumb"><a href="/resources/">Resources</a><span>/</span><span>Delivery planning</span></nav><h1>Shipping CNC parts<br/>internationally</h1><p class="sh-subtitle">A quotation checklist</p><p>Include the destination and required arrival date in your RFQ. Packing, documents and transport responsibilities need to be agreed alongside the machining work.</p><a class="sh-button" href="#section-2">See the shipping checklist</a></div><figure data-image-origin="AI-generated"><img src="/media/editorial/packing-protection-illustrative-v2-1200.webp" srcset="/media/editorial/packing-protection-illustrative-v2-480.webp 480w, /media/editorial/packing-protection-illustrative-v2-800.webp 800w, /media/editorial/packing-protection-illustrative-v2-1200.webp 1200w, /media/editorial/packing-protection-illustrative-v2-1536.webp 1536w" sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw, 52vw" width="1536" height="1024" fetchpriority="high" alt="Illustration of CNC parts separated by foam, with protective caps on threaded features"/><figcaption>AI-generated packing illustration · Not an LZZ shipment.</figcaption></figure></header>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-protection sh-section" id="section-3" aria-labelledby="protection-title"><div><p class="sh-eyebrow">Packing for international delivery</p><h2 id="protection-title">Protect finished surfaces and threads</h2><p>Packing depends on the part and transport route. Mark vulnerable surfaces and describe any receiving limits so protection can be specified in the quotation.</p></div><dl class="sh-protection-list"><div><dt>Separate and protect</dt><dd>Agree protective materials to separate parts and protect threads and mating surfaces.</dd></div><div><dt>Mark critical surfaces</dt><dd>Identify cosmetic faces, sealing surfaces, fragile edges and areas requiring cleanliness or corrosion protection.</dd></div><div><dt>Pack for the route</dt><dd>Confirm cartons or wooden cases according to the part, quantity and transport method.</dd></div><div><dt>Consider receiving limits</dt><dd>Specify pack weight or quantity limits and any handling requirements at the receiving site.</dd></div></dl></section>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-documents sh-section" id="delivery-package" aria-labelledby="documents-title"><h2 id="documents-title">Keep identification and documents together</h2><div class="sh-document-grid"><figure data-image-origin="AI-generated"><img src="/media/editorial/shipping-identification-illustrative-1200.webp" width="1200" height="800" loading="lazy" alt="Illustrative machined part with a sample identification label and paperwork"/><figcaption>AI-generated identification illustration · Not an order record.</figcaption></figure><div><h3>Part identification links to the packing list</h3><p>Provide the part number, drawing revision, quantity per pack and batch identification. Agree the label, lot-reference and inspection-document formats available for your order.</p><p>Use the same part and revision references on the packing list and agreed quality records.</p></div><div id="section-4"><h3>Agree destination-specific documents</h3><p>We provide protective packing, a packing list, commercial invoice and shipment information. Material, finishing and dimensional records are included when specified in the order.</p><p>Agree additional customs documents before production with your importing entity or freight forwarder.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="sh-transport sh-section" aria-labelledby="transport-title"><div class="sh-wrap"><p class="sh-eyebrow">Agree the delivery basis</p><h2 id="transport-title">Destination, transport and responsibilities</h2><p class="sh-transport-intro">Confirm the destination, delivery requirements and responsibilities in your quotation. EXW, FOB or DDP options are quoted for the applicable destination and service; <strong>DDP is not an automatic inclusion.</strong></p><div class="sh-transport-grid"><div><h3>Transport method</h3><p>Courier, air or sea arrangements depend on shipment size and destination. DHL, FedEx or UPS can be discussed when selecting a courier.</p></div><div><h3>Trade term and named place</h3><p>State the requested term, version and named place. Confirm who arranges transport, export/import clearance, insurance, duties, taxes and local delivery.</p></div><div><h3>Production and transit time</h3><p>Production takes <strong>7–14 business days</strong> after drawing and order confirmation, including surface finishing. Transit is estimated separately and is not included in production time.</p></div></div></div></section>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-section sh-checklist" id="section-2" aria-labelledby="checklist-title"><p class="sh-eyebrow">Shipping checklist</p><h2 id="checklist-title">Five topics to confirm before a quotation</h2><p>Use this checklist to distinguish the information you provide from the details to confirm in the quotation.</p><div class="sh-checklist-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Topic</span><span>Information you provide</span><span>Confirm in the quotation</span></div><ol>{topics.map((row,index)=><li><h3><span class="sh-number">{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span>{row[0]}</h3><div><span class="sh-mobile-label">Information you provide</span><p>{row[1]}</p></div><div><span class="sh-mobile-label">Confirm in the quotation</span><p>{row[2]}</p></div></li>)}</ol></section>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-archive" aria-labelledby="archive-title"><p class="sh-eyebrow">From the packing archive</p><h2 id="archive-title">LZZ packing archive</h2><figure><div class="sh-archive-grid">{archive.map(id=><a href={photo(id).src} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label={'View original photograph: '+photo(id).alt}><EvidenceImage id={id} sizes="(max-width:600px) 90vw, 30vw"/></a>)}</div><figcaption>LZZ packing archive · November 2022. Packing varies by part, quantity and route. These images do not establish a customer, destination, carrier, trade term or delivery outcome for a new order.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <section class="sh-wrap sh-rfq sh-section" id="section-5" aria-labelledby="rfq-title"><div><h2 id="rfq-title">Include delivery in your RFQ</h2><p>Send the controlled drawing, material and finish specification, quantity, delivery address, packing requirements, requested arrival date and document list.</p><p>Ask the quote to identify the trade term and named place, production schedule basis, transit assumption, carrier responsibility and any exclusions.</p></div><div class="sh-rfq-action"><a class="sh-button" href="/quote/">Prepare RFQ email</a><p>Review your draft before sending it from your email app.</p><a class="sh-email" href="mailto:roger@lzz-cnc.com">roger@lzz-cnc.com</a></div></section>
 <nav class="sh-wrap sh-related" aria-label="Related resources"><div><h3>Related part examples</h3><p>Each custom part requires its own drawing and quote.</p><a class="sh-secondary" href="/products/small-batch-cnc-machining-manufacturer-complex-aluminum-housings/">Complex aluminum housings</a></div><div><h3>Learn more</h3><div class="sh-related-links"><a class="sh-secondary" href="/resources/how-we-work/">How We Work</a><a class="sh-secondary" href="/resources/rfq-checklist/">RFQ Checklist</a></div></div><a class="sh-secondary" href="/resources/">Back to Resources</a></nav>
</article>
